<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><link rel="preload" as="image" href="/images/ThePoolLab.png"/><link rel="preload" as="image" href="https://brand.maytronics.com/m/4f1de64dc1be474a/EP_Large-Dolphin-Nautilus-CC-Plus-2025.webp"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="preload" as="script" fetchPriority="low" href="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin=""/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/fd9d1056-4dbbcf07a05c3f48.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/472-6eced84fcf03e6a3.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/main-app-ce281d8555633725.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/413-e7f375c310822fe5.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/reviews/%5Bsku%5D/page-158ca34b840e43ec.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js" async=""></script><title>Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus Review - The Pool Lab</title><meta name="description" content="A popular choice for many pool owners. It features clever cleaning technology and easy-to-clean filters."/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-CC-Plus"/><meta property="og:title" content="Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus Review"/><meta property="og:description" content="A popular choice for many pool owners. It features clever cleaning technology and easy-to-clean filters."/><meta property="og:image" content="https://brand.maytronics.com/m/4f1de64dc1be474a/EP_Large-Dolphin-Nautilus-CC-Plus-2025.webp"/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><meta name="twitter:title" content="The Pool Lab - Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:description" content="Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/images/ThePoolLabOG.png"/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/polyfills-c67a75d1b6f99dc8.js" crossorigin="" noModule=""></script></head><body class="d-flex flex-column min-vh-100"><nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-light bg-light"><div class="container"><a class="navbar-brand d-flex align-items-center" href="/"><div style="width:160px;height:90px;position:relative;margin-right:10px"><img src="/images/ThePoolLab.png" alt="The Pool Lab Logo" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain"/></div><span class="d-none d-sm-inline">The Pool Lab</span></a><button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#navbarNav"><span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span></button><div class="collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarNav"><ul class="navbar-nav ms-auto"><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/">Home</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/reviews">Reviews</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/best-of">Best of</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/guides">Guides</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/about">About</a></li></ul></div></div></nav><main class="flex-grow-1"><div class="container my-5"><div class="row"><div class="col-lg-8"><h1 class="mb-3">Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus<!-- -->: In-Depth Review</h1><div class="text-center mb-4 p-3 bg-white rounded border" style="height:400px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center"><img src="https://brand.maytronics.com/m/4f1de64dc1be474a/EP_Large-Dolphin-Nautilus-CC-Plus-2025.webp" alt="Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus" class="img-fluid" style="max-height:100%;max-width:100%;object-fit:contain;width:auto;height:auto"/></div><p class="lead">The Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus has cemented its status as a best-seller for a reason: it strikes the perfect balance between performance and simplicity. Designed for in-ground pools up to 50 feet, this workhorse doesn&#x27;t rely on your pool&#x27;s pump or filter, operating independently to scrub floors and walls with impressive efficiency. Its &#x27;set it and forget it&#x27; philosophy appeals to pool owners who want a sparkling clean pool without the hassle of complex programming.</p><h3 class="mt-5">Who This Is For</h3><div><p>The Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus is ideal for <strong>pool owners who value simplicity and reliability</strong> over high-tech features. It is perfect for those who want a 'plug-and-play' solution—simply drop it in and walk away.</p><p>It is best suited for:</p><ul><li><strong>In-ground pools up to 50 feet</strong> in length.</li><li>Owners who <strong>don't need smartphone control</strong> or Wi-Fi connectivity.</li><li>Anyone looking for a low-maintenance machine with <strong>easy-to-clean filters</strong>.</li><li>All pool surface types (gunite, vinyl, fiberglass, tile).</li></ul></div><h3 class="mt-5">Who Should Skip It</h3><div><p>You should skip this model if:</p><ul><li><strong>You want smart features:</strong> If you want to control your cleaner with a smartphone app or receive push notifications, look at the <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong> instead.</li><li><strong>You have a lot of fine dust/sand:</strong> While it can handle fine debris, you'll need to buy the ultra-fine filters separately. The <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong> comes with multiple filter options out of the box.</li><li><strong>You want a caddy included:</strong> This unit is heavy, and carrying it can be a chore. A caddy is an extra expense with this model.</li></ul></div><h3 class="mt-5">Key Features</h3><div><ul><li><strong>CleverClean Navigation:</strong> Smart scanning ensures complete pool coverage in a 2-hour cycle.</li><li><strong>Dual Scrubbing Brushes:</strong> Active brushing attacks algae and bacteria on floors and walls.</li><li><strong>Top-Load Filter Cartridges:</strong> Easy-access system makes cleaning the filters a breeze.</li><li><strong>Energy Efficient:</strong> Costs about 5 cents per hour to operate, independent of your pool's filtration system.</li><li><strong>Weekly Scheduler:</strong> The power supply allows you to schedule cleanings for every day, every other day, or every 3rd day.</li></ul></div><h3 class="mt-5">Detailed Analysis</h3><div><p><strong>Cleaning Performance:</strong> The Nautilus CC Plus utilizes Maytronics' <em>CleverClean</em> technology, which scans your pool to determine the most efficient path. In practice, this means it doesn't just wander aimlessly; it systematically covers the entire pool floor and climbs the walls to scrub the waterline. The dual scrubbing brushes spin twice as fast as the unit moves, effectively dislodging stuck-on algae and stubborn dirt that suction cleaners often miss.</p><p><strong>Filtration System:</strong> One of the biggest upgrades over older models is the top-load cartridge system. Instead of wrestling with a messy debris bag on the bottom of the unit, you simply pop open the top hatch and lift out the two large filter cartridges. They rinse clean in seconds with a garden hose. The standard filters are excellent for leaves and larger debris, though you might want to invest in the ultra-fine filters (sold separately) if you deal with fine dust or sand.</p><p><strong>Ease of Use:</strong> This is a true plug-and-play device. There is no assembly required. You simply plug the power supply into a standard outlet, drop the cleaner in the pool, and press the single button on the control unit. It runs a standard 2-hour cycle and then shuts off automatically. The lack of Bluetooth or Wi-Fi might be a downside for tech enthusiasts, but for most users, the simplicity is a major plus.</p><p><strong>Durability & Maintenance:</strong> The unit feels robust and well-built. The tracks provide excellent traction on gunite, vinyl, and fiberglass surfaces. Maintenance is minimal—mostly just rinsing the filters and occasionally checking the impeller for debris. However, the lack of a swivel on the 60-foot cable can lead to tangling if you don't properly coil the cord after each use.</p></div><div class="row mt-4"><div class="col-md-6"><div class="card border-success h-100"><div class="card-header bg-success text-white">Pros</div><ul class="list-group list-group-flush"><li class="list-group-item">Outstanding wall-climbing and waterline scrubbing</li><li class="list-group-item">Top-access filters are incredibly easy to clean</li><li class="list-group-item">Simple plug-and-play operation with no setup</li><li class="list-group-item">Weekly scheduler function built into the power supply</li><li class="list-group-item">Energy efficient and quiet operation</li></ul></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="card border-danger h-100"><div class="card-header bg-danger text-white">Cons</div><ul class="list-group list-group-flush"><li class="list-group-item">Cable lacks a swivel, leading to occasional tangling</li><li class="list-group-item">Does not include a caddy (sold separately)</li><li class="list-group-item">No smartphone app or remote control features</li><li class="list-group-item">Ultra-fine filters for sand/silt must be purchased separately</li></ul></div></div></div><h3 class="mt-5">Final Verdict</h3><p>The Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus is the &#x27;Goldilocks&#x27; of robotic pool cleaners—it&#x27;s just right for the vast majority of pool owners. It skips the fancy bells and whistles like Wi-Fi and remote steering in favor of raw cleaning power and reliability. If you want a cleaner that you can drop in the pool and trust to do a fantastic job every single time, this is the one to buy. It&#x27;s a solid investment that pays for itself in time saved and chemical costs reduced.</p></div><div class="col-lg-4"><div class="card sticky-top" style="top:20px"><div class="card-body text-center"><h5 class="card-title">Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus</h5><p class="card-text">Ready to buy? Get the best price online.</p><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00Q8M0NWE?tag=scorpiusllc-20" target="_blank" class="btn btn-warning btn-lg fw-bold w-100 ">Check Price on Amazon</a><small class="text-muted d-block mt-2">We may earn a commission on qualifying purchases.</small></div><div class="card mt-4"><div class="card-header bg-light fw-bold">Consider These Alternatives</div><ul class="list-group list-group-flush"><li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center"><a class="text-decoration-none fw-bold" href="/reviews/Dolphin-Premier">Dolphin Premier</a><span class="badge bg-secondary rounded-pill">$<!-- -->1599</span></li><li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center"><a class="text-decoration-none fw-bold" href="/reviews/Polaris-9650iQ-Sport">Polaris 9650iQ Sport</a><span class="badge bg-secondary rounded-pill">$<!-- -->1099</span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></main><footer class="bg-dark text-white text-center py-3 mt-auto"><div class="container"><p class="mb-1">© <!-- -->2026<!-- --> <!-- -->The Pool Lab<!-- -->. All rights reserved.</p><small class="text-white-50">The Pool Lab<!-- --> is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com.</small></div></footer><script src="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin="" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0]);self.__next_f.push([2,null])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:HL[\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n2:HL[\"/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css\",\"sty